From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:52:10 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: remove the receive delivery nothing can bind to

The buffer manager carries a receive demultiplexer: a table of network
devices indexed by the source port the packet MAC records in a received
frame's header, and a delivery tail that copies the frame into a socket
buffer and hands it to the stack.

Nothing fills that table. Its one setter has no caller anywhere in the
tree, so the bound mask stays zero, the delivery test never passes and
not one frame has ever taken the tail. The processor's end of this
datapath is a network device of its own, and it terminates its macro's
receive ring directly rather than through the buffer manager.

Remove the table, its setter, the source-port resolver and the delivery
tail. The bottom half still drains the load spreader's output and
returns every segment it finds to the free-segment pool, so a descriptor
that does arrive is accounted for rather than leaked.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

